comments.body:
A change to this for Pi in 2f5a3f1c0 (v0.1.2187): Pi's own `models.json` keeps Gemini models on Chat again. OmO and Prime Agent still use `google-generative-ai`.

Why: other apps load Pi's agent folder through Pi's SDK too. Raft (slock, `@botiverse/raft-daemon`, pi-ai 0.83.0) opens `~/.pi/agent/models.json` and gives every request its own `fetch`. pi-ai's Google adapter throws on that before it sends anything: "Custom fetch is not supported by the Google Generative AI adapter". pi-ai 1.4.0 does the same. So since v0.1.2042, every Gemini model failed in Raft (reported on X). Raft can't change what it reads, so the file has to work for both. On Chat, the gateway translates the request to Gemini, the same as before v0.1.2042.

@XYenon, if you see something that only works on `google-generative-ai` (a field that is dropped), please say so here, and we'll fix it in the translation.

